 SG_ ECU_PRESENT : 52|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" CONN,LINUX



CM_ "moto-platform platform CAN bus (classic CAN 500 kbps, 11-bit IDs). ID plan and E2E rules: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md section 4. Single source of truth; consumers use gen/ output only.";
CM_ BU_ RT_CORE "Node ID 1. STM32H7 domain controller. Sole vehicle-bus tester (D-021); republishes decoded vehicle signals here.";
CM_ BU_ SAFETY "Node ID 2. STM32G4 cornering safety decision (isolated).";
CM_ BU_ IO "Node ID 3. STM32G0 blind spot, immobilizer, power management.";
CM_ BU_ CONN "Node ID 4. ESP32-S3 Wi-Fi/BLE/voice.";
CM_ BU_ LINUX "Node ID 5. Raspberry Pi 5 (Kuksa via kuksa-can-provider).";
CM_ BU_ HIL_SIM "Node ID 0xE. HIL restbus simulator.";
CM_ BU_ TESTER "Node ID 0xF. External diagnostic tester.";
CM_ BO_ 32 "rt-core EKF (Layer 2) lean estimate for the cornering decision. Safety range, E2E protected.";
CM_ SG_ 32 LEAN_ANGLE "Roll angle, ISO 8855: positive = right side down.";
CM_ SG_ 32 LEAN_RATE "Roll rate, ISO 8855: positive = rolling to the right.";
CM_ SG_ 32 LEAN_ANGLE_QUALITY "EKF confidence in LEAN_ANGLE, 0 = none, 100 = full.";
CM_ SG_ 32 LEAN_STATUS "0 = NOT_AVAILABLE so an all-zero payload is never valid. Codes 5-15 are invalid. Whether CLAMPED/DEFAULT_FALLBACK may be used by the safety decision is open (Q-002).";
CM_ BO_ 33 "rt-core EKF (Layer 2) cornering parameters, clamped to physical ranges by rt-core. Safety range, E2E protected.";
CM_ SG_ 33 FRICTION_COEFF "Estimated tyre-road friction coefficient (mu). The DBC range is a transport range, not a safety ceiling: safety-node applies its own fixed ceiling.";
CM_ SG_ 33 TOTAL_MASS "Estimated vehicle + rider + load mass. Transport range only; physically implausible values (e.g. 0) mean INVALID at the consumer, never clamped (plausibility limits to be set with Q-002).";
CM_ SG_ 33 COG_HEIGHT "Estimated centre-of-gravity height above ground. Transport range only; implausible values (e.g. 0) mean INVALID at the consumer.";
CM_ SG_ 33 PARAM_QUALITY "EKF confidence in the parameters, 0 = none, 100 = full.";
CM_ SG_ 33 PARAM_STATUS "0 = NOT_AVAILABLE so an all-zero payload is never valid. Codes 5-15 are invalid. Use of CLAMPED/DEFAULT_FALLBACK values is open (Q-002).";
CM_ BO_ 48 "Vehicle speed republished by rt-core from the CL250 ECU (uds/vehicle_cl250.yaml DID 0xF40D, D-021). Consumed by safety-node, so safety range and E2E protected.";
CM_ SG_ 48 VEHICLE_SPEED_STATUS "0 = NOT_AVAILABLE so an all-zero payload is never valid. VALID only while the polled source value is younger than twice its poll period (uds/vehicle_cl250.yaml; 1600 ms at the current 800 ms), else STALE. rt-core keeps sending at the cycle time. E2E proves frame freshness, not value freshness; whether that source age is acceptable for the safety decision is open (Q-002).";
CM_ BO_ 129 "Heartbeat of RT_CORE (0x080 + node ID 1). Monitored by safety-node.";
CM_ BO_ 130 "Heartbeat of SAFETY (0x080 + node ID 2).";
CM_ BO_ 131 "Heartbeat of IO (0x080 + node ID 3).";
CM_ BO_ 132 "Heartbeat of CONN (0x080 + node ID 4).";
CM_ BO_ 133 "Heartbeat of LINUX (0x080 + node ID 5).";
CM_ BO_ 272 "CL250 powertrain values republished by rt-core from polled ECU DIDs (uds/vehicle_cl250.yaml, D-021). Each *_VALID bit is 1 only while that value is fresh.";
CM_ SG_ 272 ECU_PRESENT "1 while the engine ECU answered any request within ecu_absent_timeout_ms.";
